# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_version_honesty.py" "VERSION HONESTY GATE: PASS" "version honesty (/healthz reports the build it is actually running)" "version honesty: /healthz reports WHICH COMMIT is live, DERIVED from the git commit baked at build time -- never a hand-bumped env (VERIPSA_VERSION) that goes stale the instant you deploy (the old bug: a health endpoint that misreported the live build, confusing even the operator). health_watchdog.build_version() resolves VERIPSA_BUILD_SHA env (the Dockerfile turns the GIT_SHA build arg into it) -> the baked /app/BUILD_SHA file -> the legacy VERIPSA_VERSION override -> 'dev'. The derived sha STRICTLY beats the legacy env (a deploy can never be masked by a stale manual label). DEGRADES, never crashes: with no source at all it returns an honest 'dev' and health_snapshot() still builds. content-free (a short, trimmed commit sha -- no path/secret shape)" "version honesty: /healthz reports the live build derived from the git commit (build sha env -> baked BUILD_SHA file -> legacy env -> 'dev'); the derived sha beats a stale manual label, and it degrades to 'dev' without crashing when no source is set" 16
